    {
      "id": "rufin-rubens",
      "name": "Rufin Rubens",
      "sourceType": "immersive_npc_roster",
      "sourceFile": "NPC Rosters.docx",
      "province": "Kaelvorrin",
      "provinceKey": "kaelvorrin",
      "settlement": "Mistval",
      "settlementKey": "kaelvorrin:Mistval",
      "description": "Rufin Rubens is a Dwarf repairman with nimble hands, tavern gossip, and a talent for finding uses for machines everyone else left rusting in basements. He fixes locks, boilers, drink lines, lift gears, caravan carts, and temperamental constructs for the Brass Concordat, usually while pretending the job is easier than it is. Rufin is practical and friendly, but when old machines are tied to ichor, alcohol, or missing people, he starts asking questions no one hired him to ask.",
      "settlementAndAncestryTexture": "Mistval is a City in Kaelvorrin, under Consensus Democracy, with low danger, Farming, Treetops - treehouses, Grassland terrain. Local records favor Altruistic, Lawful, Cooperative, Honorable civic habits; common communities include Human, Halfling — Lightfoot Halfling, Halfling — Stout Halfling, Kender, Kithkin. Dwarf reads through the Dwarf entry of the race compendium, within Dwarven and Gnomish Kin, marked by Marduthor. Dwarves are stout, resilient folk deeply tied to stone, craft, and ancestral tradition. They value honor, craftsmanship, and enduring legacies over fleeting trends. Table cues: Darkvision, Dwarven Resilience, Dwarven Toughness, Stonecunning; starting tendency Neutral - Lawful - Cooperative - Honorable.",
      "rumors": [
        "Rufin can identify a tavern's owner by the shortcuts in its pipe repairs.",
        "He has a list of old brewing constructs that were never properly decommissioned."
      ],
      "plotHooks": [
        "Rufin sends the party to retrieve a mobile brewer before its recipes poison an entire inn district.",
        "A broken service construct recognizes Rufin and accuses him of abandoning a delivery decades ago."
      ],
